    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "description": "MH-internal forward latency, decomposed. The three phases have DIFFERENT REMEDIES, which is why an undifferentiated total is not enough: `receive_buffer` (received -> ingress pop) means the forward loop is not keeping up with the receive loop; `processing` (ingress pop -> egress push) is MH's own routing and relay rewrite; `transmit_buffer` (egress push -> send returned) is a slow subscriber. `total` exists solely to serve the objective, because quantiles do not sum and cannot be reconstructed from the three. THE 30 ms OBJECTIVE IS PROVISIONAL: ADR-0011's figure is not ratified against this measurement point, which is MH-internal rather than end to end. Story 8 ratifies it. NO BURN-RATE ALERT MAY REST ON IT UNTIL THEN (docs/observability/slos.md). SAMPLED ONE-IN-N: read the sample-ratio panel beside this one before reading any rate off _count, which is 1/N of mh_media_frames_forwarded_total - dividing the two directly measures the sample ratio, not the media path. A FLAT PANEL IS AMBIGUOUS AND ALWAYS WILL BE: this family reads present-and-flat-at-zero both when the handler is idle and when no media session ever started, and the two are byte-identical here. Discriminate with Media Session Starts by Outcome first, then with mh_media_frames_dropped_total{reason=\"transport_receive_dropped\"} - flat means no datagram ever arrived, moving means MH received them and never read them. See docs/observability/metrics/mh-service.md \u00a7Media Forward Path.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "Seconds",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false,
              "legend": false
            },
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "$datasource"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by(le, phase) (rate(mh_media_forward_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{phase}} p95",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Media Forward Latency by Phase (p95) - OBJECTIVE PROVISIONAL",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "description": "The fraction of forwarded frames whose latency is observed. Published from THE SAME configuration field the sampler draws against (MH_MEDIA_LATENCY_SAMPLE_RATIO, optional, code default 0.01), so it cannot drift from the ratio in force. This is INTERPRETATION INPUT for the latency panel, not a health signal: it has no target and no threshold. Not to be confused with OTEL_SAMPLE_RATE, which is trace head-sampling. See docs/observability/dashboard-conventions.md \u00a7Periodicity. A FLAT PANEL IS AMBIGUOUS AND ALWAYS WILL BE: this family reads present-and-flat-at-zero both when the handler is idle and when no media session ever started, and the two are byte-identical here. Discriminate with Media Session Starts by Outcome first, then with mh_media_frames_dropped_total{reason=\"transport_receive_dropped\"} - flat means no datagram ever arrived, moving means MH received them and never read them. See docs/observability/metrics/mh-service.md \u00a7Media Forward Path.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
