      "description": "MH's OWN application egress queue depth, in frames \u2014 not quinn's send buffer. TREND ONLY: no alert may rest on this panel alone, and it is one process-wide gauge fed by N per-subscriber queues (last writer wins), so a saturated queue can be masked by an idle one. The countable signal is mh_media_frames_dropped_total{reason=\"egress_queue_overflow\"}. Both caveats and the reasoning behind them are stated once in docs/observability/metrics/mh-service.md \u00a7Media Forward Path; this description points at it rather than restating it, because the two dashboards had already drifted on the wording. A FLAT PANEL IS AMBIGUOUS AND ALWAYS WILL BE: this family reads present-and-flat-at-zero both when the handler is idle and when no media session ever started, and the two are byte-identical here. Discriminate with Media Session Starts by Outcome first, then with mh_media_frames_dropped_total{reason=\"transport_receive_dropped\"} - flat means no datagram ever arrived, moving means MH received them and never read them. See docs/observability/metrics/mh-service.md \u00a7Media Forward Path.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
